431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Our venture aims to address the challenges faced by patients by developing a portable, non-invasive device that utilizes air puff technology to measure IOP. This solution will offer a more patient-friendly approach, reducing discomfort while enabling frequent monitoring outside of clinical environments. By making glaucoma detection and IOP measurement more accessible, our device has the potential to revolutionize early diagnosis and long-term management of the disease, ultimately reducing the global burden of blindness caused by glaucoma.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
