/T (Traditional IOP measurement techniques, such as Goldmann applanation tonometry, require direct contact with the eye. This process is uncomfortable, can cause infection, and must be performed by trained professionals, restricting the frequency of testing. The lack of portable, non-invasive solutions further exacerbates accessibility challenges, hindering early detection and monitoring of glaucoma.)
